-- Migration to v5: wipes existing `level` and `progress` data ahead of the difficulty-tiered
-- pack regeneration (GAME_DESIGN.md §9g, §5). Levels 1-50 are being regenerated with new
-- per-tier parameters (grid size/word count/scrambleMoves now vary by level number instead of
-- one fixed set for the whole pack) -- level *content* changes under the same level number
-- (different grid layout, different target words, different move limit), so any existing
-- `progress` row (stars, best-moves) recorded against the OLD content would silently misdescribe
-- the new content under the same level number rather than merely going stale.
--
-- Decision (see GAME_DESIGN.md §9g for the full reasoning): wipe both tables outright rather than
-- attempt to reconcile or preserve old progress. This is pre-launch -- there is no real user data
-- to protect -- and a kept-but-stale star rating would be actively misleading, not just imprecise,
-- since it'd be displayed against a puzzle the player never actually solved in that form. This is
-- a one-time, one-off decision tied to this specific regeneration, not a standing policy for
-- future content changes.
--
-- `progress` alone would be enough to reset the main menu's aggregate stats (totalWordsFound/
-- currentDayStreak, see ProgressRepository) since both are computed live from `progress` joined
-- against `level`, not stored as separate counters -- wiping `level` too is what then makes
-- `LevelRepository.seedPackIfNeeded`'s idempotent-by-count-check (`countForLanguage(language) >=
-- LEVEL_PACK_SIZE`) re-trigger a real reseed on next app start, producing the new tiered content
-- rather than leaving the old fixed-parameter pack in place.
DELETE FROM progress;
DELETE FROM level;
